      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "RIVER STORM (1) enjoyed a class drop last time out and scored over 1609m at Geelong, getting home by 5.4 metres to make it two wins from his last three starts. Led from wider there so can take full advantage of the inside draw. CAPTAIN MOONLIGHT NZ (11) is a progressive former Kiwi who made it two wins in a row at this venue when he came from this same barrier to score narrowly over this distance a fortnight ago. With even luck he can make an impact again. MONTANA PRIDE (2) ended last prep with a series of close-up efforts. Hasn't raced for nine weeks but has won when fresh before and draws well so is capable of a forward showing. GUNFORHIRE (10) cops a tricky draw but is a player with luck having come from the back row for third here last week.",
